.Dd November 6, 2026
.Dt MBT_WEBSEED 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mbt_torrent_add_webseed ,
.Nm mbt_torrent_webseed_bytes ,
.Nm mbt_http_curl_range_fn ,
.Nm mbt_http_curl_range_cancel ,
.Nm mbt_http_curl_set_ca ,
.Nm mbt_http_curl_set_low_speed
.Nd BEP 19 web seeds
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In mbt/torrent.h
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_torrent_add_webseed "struct mbt_torrent *t" "const char *url"
.Ft uint64_t
.Fn mbt_torrent_webseed_bytes "struct mbt_torrent *t"
.In mbt/http_curl.h
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_http_curl_set_ca "struct mbt_http_curl *c" "const void *pem" "size_t len"
.Ft void
.Fn mbt_http_curl_set_low_speed "struct mbt_http_curl *c" "long bytes_per_sec" "long sec"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A web seed is an HTTP or HTTPS server with the torrent's file.
Only single-file torrents use web seeds.
The session reads
.Dq url-list
from a .torrent file.
.Fn mbt_torrent_add_webseed
adds one more URL.
A URL that ends in a slash gets the torrent name.
A torrent holds at most 16 URLs, and it does not save them.
.Pp
A web seed needs the
.Fa http_range
and
.Fa http_range_cancel
hooks in
.Vt struct mbt_session_config .
Without them, the session ignores web seeds.
.Fn mbt_http_curl_range_fn
and
.Fn mbt_http_curl_range_cancel
are these hooks for libcurl.
.Fn mbt_http_curl_set_ca
sets the CA list from memory, for a process that cannot read CA files.
.Pp
A web seed sends one request at a time, for a run of contiguous pieces.
It claims each piece as its bytes arrive, so peers can take the rest of the run.
If a peer has the next piece, the web seed ends the request.
Each piece gets a hash check like a piece from a peer.
.Fn mbt_torrent_webseed_bytes
returns the bytes received from web seeds.
.Sh POLICY
.Vt struct mbt_webseed_policy
sets when web seeds run.
It is in the session configuration and in
.Vt struct mbt_add_torrent_cfg .
A torrent with mode
.Dv MBT_WEBSEED_DEFAULT
uses the session policy.
A session with that mode uses
.Dv MBT_WEBSEED_FALLBACK ,
a 5 second
.Fa no_peer_delay_ms ,
a 10 second
.Fa low_rate_delay_ms ,
and a
.Fa low_rate
of 64 KiB per second.
With any other mode, each field is used as given, and 0 is valid.
.Pp
A run is 5 percent of the file, within
.Fa run_min
and
.Fa run_max .
With a rate limit, a run is one piece.
For these two fields, 0 means 4 MiB and 64 MiB.
Set both to the piece length for one piece in each request.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Dv MBT_WEBSEED_OFF
Web seeds do not run.
.It Dv MBT_WEBSEED_FALLBACK
Web seeds take pieces after
.Fa no_peer_delay_ms
with no connected peer, or after
.Fa low_rate_delay_ms
below
.Fa low_rate
from peers.
They also start if all trackers answered with no peers and DHT is off.
They stop taking pieces when peers are fast again.
.It Dv MBT_WEBSEED_ALWAYS
Web seeds always take pieces.
.El
.Pp
.Fa webseed_max_requests
limits the range requests in a session.
The default is 16.
.Sh FAILURES
A hash mismatch, or HTTP status 404 or 410, drops the URL for the session.
Other failures wait from 5 seconds up to 5 minutes, and honor Retry-After.
A dropped URL does not fail the torrent.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn mbt_torrent_add_webseed
returns 0, or
.Er EINVAL
as a negative value if the URL is not http or https, or
.Er ENOSPC
as a negative value if the torrent has 16 URLs.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mbt_session 3 ,
.Xr mbt_storage 3
